### Existing system workflows

For accounting, finance or an integration task, read the applicable canonical
system skill before choosing its data route. Use the project skill list and
`AGENTS.md` routing; select only an existing project-scoped workflow with the
matching published system name. Never construct arbitrary file paths from
remote capability keys.

An advertised capability and its installed system workflow are independent of
`system_catalog`. Missing or unknown general catalog support does not invalidate
a fixed authenticated RPC route explicitly documented by that workflow. Stop
only the unsupported catalog read, then follow the relevant workflow for the
human's actual task. A capability advertises support, not a connected account.
The system workflow owns any explicit connection-status or provider-data read.
Do not guess method names, use general finance chat as a substitute, or ask the
human to create a new conversation or repeat the routing instruction.

A requested list of systems may report advertised support without reading
provider records. Only a task explicitly needing those records proceeds to its
system workflow; a plain bootstrap does not read them.
